WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
*siren*

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.980
Well that does it, time for the purge.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.740
For the next 12 hours, all crime is legal!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.360
I'm so excited, this is gonna be the perfect night!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.580
Oh, what do you have planned?

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.260
Looting?

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.500
Murder?

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.920
What? No, I'm gonna pirate episodes of "Great British Baking Show" and then tinker with the YouTube algorithm.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.380
And heck, if there's time we can even maybe steal the recipe for Diet Coke and be in bed by 11!

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.320
That does sound like the perfect night.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.220
It does!

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:31.980
Clink!

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.200
*gunshot*

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.800
Hello internet!

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.360
Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.540
The show that strives to purge every ounce of fun and whimsy from all the movies that you love.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.840
Today we're taking a stab at "The Purge" franchise,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.460
which if you haven't seen, is actually really interesting in terms of premise.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:01.720
It's set in an alternate future where Americans are entitled to 12 hours of purging every year.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:08.440
Starting at 7pm every March 21st, all crime in the US is legal, lasting until 7am the following morning.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:14.680
"Commencing at the siren, any and all crime, including murder, will be legal for 12 continuous hours."

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.880
And as you might expect, "The Purge" franchise really digs in,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.660
exploring all sorts of creative crimes that people might choose to commit,

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.600
if there were indeed no laws for the night.

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:25.480
Just kidding!

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.320
It is just a bunch of killing!

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.900
Murder, murder, murder.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.640
Sure, there's a bit of vandalism and looting sprinkled in for flavor, but come on!

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.560
You're telling me that all crime is legal for 12 hours,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.540
and nobody is using that opportunity to do anything interesting with it?

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.860
Where's all your creativity, people?

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:45.740
Rigged gambling, hacking, insider trading,

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.280
Why are we not following the people who are trying to make themselves filthy stinking rich?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.250
With all this focus on murder and petty looting, you're wasting such a cool premise!

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.580
You have 12 heours each year to change your life,

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.800
or heck, improve the lives of your family, friends, society itself,

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.419
and you use it all to smash a few windows!

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.000
Think big picture here, people!

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.080
So that, loyal theorists, is our question today.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:15.520
Not how to survive The Purge, but how you WIN The Purge?

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.400
What is the best use of that 12 hour window,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.040
because, let's face it, what started as a pretty wacky film series

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.380
is starting to feel more and more possible every day,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.440
and we need to be prepared.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.720
You know what, I'm gonna be honest.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.270
When I first embarked on this thought experiment,

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:33.060
I assumed that developing the perfect purge strategy would be pretty darn easy.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.360
All I had to do is figure out what high-yield crimes would be safely carried out in one night,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.860
hire some hackers or whatever, and then profit.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.660
But when you actually start thinking through the logistics of this stuff,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.400
things actually get a lot more complicated.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.079
Because remember, when all crime is legal,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.360
It's legal for everyone. That becomes a two-way street.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.640
Say for instance, you figure out a way to cheat a casino, and you want to cash in.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.300
A few loaded dice or a stacked deck in your hand,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.640
sounds like a fun (and profitable) way to spend the Purge night, right?

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.600
No problem.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.960
Well, yes big problem.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.480
For those 12 hours, not only can you cheat the casino,

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.660
the casino is legally allowed to rig the game against you.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.179
And with them controlling the cards,

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.160
the deck is definitely stacked against you.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.920
Here's another one, say you want to rob a bank vault.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.960
Well, you're gonna need associates for your heist.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.040
But make sure that you trust those guys,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.260
since, you know, they can always pull a "Dark Knight" and just off you at the end of the evening,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.340
and take the loot for themselves.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.820
It's actually something that we see in "The Purge" movies.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.420
Remember how well it works when criminals work with other criminals in those films?

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.780
Not super great,

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.260
but then again that might be the least of your worries,

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.240
considering that the bank guards themselves are suddenly legally able to straight-up murder you.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.000
Again, it's no rules for everyone.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.140
When developing the perfect purge strategy,

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.140
you also have to remember that The Purge is a yearly event,

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.960
so you don't want to be committing a crime that's gonna screw someone over and then be traced back to you,

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.560
since a year from now it's gonna leave a big old target on your back.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.940
Market manipulation, insider trading, identity theft, embezzlement.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.300
These can all be traced back to you, because they're being done online.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.940
Committing these sorts of crimes during The Purge

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.659
doesn't really offer you that much additional cover than any other day of the year.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.800
Sure, the US government might choose not to prosecute you,

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.100
since your crime occurred during that window of opportunity,

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.420
but does that really matter when you've stolen a ton of money,

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.000
from presumably wealthy well-connected powerful people?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:26.900
Come next year's Purge,

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.740
you could find yourself at the receiving end of some extremely well-funded vigilante justice.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.780
Or, to demonstrate one last example of the complicating factors of The Purge,

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:38.920
say you want to spend that time counterfeiting US currency,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.869
or you have a bunch of counterfeit currency and you want to use it, great!

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.420
It's a plan that literally is printing money.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.950
But you spending that cash is actually gonna happen outside of The Purge window,

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.960
Meaning that once again, you're a criminal.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.280
Try to deposit it in a bank?

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.540
Too bad you can't, it's too late in the day.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.240
And honestly, the bank doesn't have to do it.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.220
Legally, they're not responsible for that.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:02.959
And if you could do any of this, there's one other layer that we have to take into account here.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.640
Sure, national laws may be suspended, but what about international laws?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.040
US laws may turn a blind eye for 12 hours,

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.120
but international laws won't.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:18.240
The 1929 Geneva Convention made the counterfeiting of any currency illegal in every country.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:21.439
So even if you didn't technically do anything illegal in the US,

00:05:21.439 --> 00:05:25.038
you'd still be breaking the law in a ton of other countries,

00:05:25.038 --> 00:05:29.540
and come 7am the next morning, the USA's extradition treaties are back in effect.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:30.980
International money laundering,

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.268
tax evasion schemes,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.620
big old nopes there, too.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:38.720
So at this point, I feel like I should pause and offer an apology to James DeMonaco,

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.140
the writer, director and producer of "The Purge".

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.040
Before I began researching this topic,

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.520
I figured "The Purge" franchise was well, I thought it was kind of dumb.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:51.380
Fun, yeah, absolutely, but definitely dumb just mindless popcorn fodder.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:57.280
I'll admit it, the fact that all "The Purge" characters pretty much stuck to was murder, just kind of felt cheap,

00:05:57.289 --> 00:06:01.200
It's like they weren't behaving like real people would in this scenario,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.660
and instead were just doing a bunch of fun-to-watch crimes,

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.400
for no other reason that they were in a violent horror movie.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.720
It felt like lazy writing,

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.800
and I was oh-so-ready to poke holes in the wishy-washy legalese of it all with hypotheticals,

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:17.260
like "What if you shoot someone at 6:59, but they don't die until 7:01?"

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.360
"Will the government still prosecute you then?"

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.020
or "What if you're caught in possession of stolen property the day after The Purge, what then?"

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.840
but what I came to realize is that it's all fairly simple.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:27.780
None of that matters.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.720
Whether or not the government's gonna prosecute you

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.980
for crimes that occur outside that 12 hour window hardly matters,

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.600
because the true judgment, and the true threat,

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.980
is ultimately coming from your fellow man.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:43.600
The people that you've wronged will have a chance to get even on March 21st the following year.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.560
Or there's always the international authorities who'd like to get even as well,

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.678
so to truly win The Purge,

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.560
we need a highly profitable crime,

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.660
that can be over and done with within that 12 hour window,

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.340
a crime that isn't governed by international law,

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.160
and doesn't rely on us screwing over other people,

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.560
or leave us open to the reverse.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.878
Or if we are taking advantage of someone, they can't be left alive to know about it.

00:07:04.879 --> 00:07:05.779
So at this point,

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:10.800
you're probably starting to wonder if there's any crime out there that won't get you targeted in a future Purge.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.540
And the answer is: Yeah, sure. There are tons of crimes that you can commit that would benefit society.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.420
Filling potholes without a permit,

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.200
trespassing on a private beach to pick up trash,

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:20.800
ooooo!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.980
These are victimless crimes,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:23.980
but they're not gonna make you rich,

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.040
and if we're aiming for the perfect Purge,

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.200
well, we need it all.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:32.640
But what? What is a victimless crime that could benefit society and get you rich at the same time?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.310
Theorists, I thought about this for a long time,

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:38.580
I looked deep inside of myself for a solution,

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.249
and wouldn't you know it I found that solution there, deep within me.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.600
In fact, I found lots of solutions deep within me.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.460
Literally.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.680
That's right, I'm talking organ harvesting.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:55.140
Consider this: a legal healthy human heart is valued at a million dollars.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:08:00.300
A million dollars for your heart, and that is just one organ.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:04.480
Now on any other night of the year, human organs wouldn't be readily available,

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.560
and you wouldn't be legally allowed to sell them.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:07.420
But guess what?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.660
On Purge Night, it's no rules, just right,

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.440
just like an Outback Steakhouse.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.069
We know from... well, pretty much every "Purge" movie,

00:08:15.069 --> 00:08:21.860
But let's call out "Purge: Election Year" that a whole bunch of dead bodies just lie around in the streets until 7am the next morning.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:27.740
We see this very explicitly as Laney and  Dawn spend The Purge driving around in an armored ambulance,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.360
carefully considering who to help,

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.000
but instead of focusing on the living,

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.200
what if instead we chose to focus on the dead?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.848
Could Laney and Dawn have found something that we could capitalize off of?

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:42.480
I'm thinking so cuz we could use that same armored ambulance idea to collect the dead.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.640
"Bring out your dead!"

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:47.780
And bring those freshly killed Purgers to hospitals,

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.360
or at the very least, our gang of waiting doctors and nurses,

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:56.820
where the organs in the body could then be harvested by trained medical professionals in proper facilities.

00:08:56.959 --> 00:08:59.700
Now normally, this would be totally illegal.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:04.419
Commercial harvesting and selling of body parts is illegal in all countries, except Iran.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:08.220
But on Purge Night, those concerns go out the window,

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:13.540
and you see, these organs are incredibly valuable, in every sense of that word.

00:09:13.546 --> 00:09:14.529
In the US alone,

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:19.560
there are more than 113,000 candidates waiting for transplants,

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:23.620
and many are willing to pay whatever it takes to get access to that life-saving organ,

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.679
which has, in turn, created a black market for some of the stuff.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:29.840
This is especially true for kidney transplants.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.409
Humans are born with two, but they only need one,

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:37.780
so the selling of your second kidney to people who need it is something that really does exist out there in the world.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:42.240
And the idea of using the recently dead as organ donors isn't a new idea, either.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:44.680
People can sign up to be organ donors for after they die,

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:50.040
and in China, inmates executed on death row were historically used as organ donors.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.950
So let's talk brass tacks: how much is one dead body on Purge Night going to net us?

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:58.420
Well, unfortunately, we have to discount some of the most valuable organs right out of the gate.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.880
A heart is normally useless after death,

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.780
so we're gonna have to kiss that million dollars I mentioned earlier goodbye.

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.960
The liver also breaks down pretty quickly after cardiac arrest,

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.000
so we're not gonna be able to pawn that one either.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.380
Some relatively small ticket items will last a bit longer,

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.680
like the skin, which collectively might be around $5000.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.440
The corneas in your eye will be worth significantly more if undamaged,

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.320
at about $20,000.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.220
And those kidneys that I mentioned before?

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.200
They're going for about $262,000.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.280
Not too shabby for an organ we got two of,

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:32.460
but the real big-ticket item here is something that goes deeper than all those: bone marrow.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:37.160
Bone marrow is by far the most valuable substance by weight in the human body,

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:41.620
at an incredible $23,000 per gram.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.940
Per gram!

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.700
And the human body, oh boy, does it have a lot of the stuff.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:54.280
The average full-grown human male is walking around with about 2.6 kilograms of bone marrow in their body.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:11:00.820
That is nearly $60 million of bone marrow just sitting there in your chair right now,

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.279
and here some of you thought that you weren't worth that much.

00:11:03.459 --> 00:11:05.120
So this then begs the obvious question of

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.180
"Why isn't everyone rushing down to the hospital right now,

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.700
to sell off a tiny piece of their body, and buy a new house or something?"

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.920
Well in most states, it's illegal.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:18.600
In California for instance, you can be compensated up to $3,000 for the procedure.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:22.400
So there is an upper limit to what you could be earning legally from this sort of stuff,

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:26.019
and you see, for as huge as some of these numbers are, that's the overall rub.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:29.140
These are the real prices of these organs:

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:30.440
million dollars for a heart,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.960
quarter million for a kidney,

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.060
a bunch for bone marrow.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:36.500
But in reality, if you were to sell this stuff, they're not netting that high of a price.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.229
According to medical transcription estimates,

00:11:38.229 --> 00:11:44.280
the average price a dead human body is likely gonna be more around $550,000.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:48.320
Still, half a million dollars for each person that you pick up off the street?

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.520
Not too bad!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.380
On Purge Night, those streets are paved in gold.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:56.020
Fleshy, cadaverous, recently murdered gold...

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:59.420
And that, my friends, is the recipe for the perfect Purge.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:03.900
Like I said, in the US alone, there's currently over 100,000 people waiting for organs,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:08.000
but only about 14,000 organs get donated every year.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:08.900
But with this plan,

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:12.160
A. There's no victim, because they were already dead in the street,

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.240
B. You and your team of medical professionals are actually working

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:18.920
to help save some of the people on that 100,000 person wait list,

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.940
and C. Harvesting and selling organs to hospitals,

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.700
or on the black market or whatever you end up doing in that 12-hour window,

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.960
could net you a ton of cash,

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.820
maybe as much as $550,000 per body that you pick up.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:37.940
See, most people might use The Purge to settle vendettas, or enrich themselves financially,

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.149
but are these selfish people really doing The Purge right?

00:12:40.149 --> 00:12:44.380
The Purge is an opportunity to give the gift of life to otherwise hopeless people,

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.160
by circumventing society's red tape.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:53.720
For a connoisseur that's looking to purge perfectly, those 12 hours aren't just an opportunity to get rich,

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:56.420
it's an opportunity to make a difference.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:01.860
And that is doing The Purge right, that my friends, is the perfect Purge.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:05.120
But hey! That's just a theory.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.659
A Film Theory!

00:13:07.659 --> 00:13:08.330
Aaaaaand...

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.360
one last thing, actually.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.980
Being a blood or bone marrow donor really does help save lives.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.800
Heck, I'm gonna go out on a limb here,

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:19.220
and tell you that I'm personally signed up to be an organ donor for when I die.

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.380
I mean, my eyes are terrible sight-wise,

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:28.040
but if my corneas can help someone see for the first time or repair damage to their eye, then great.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:28.760
Awesome!

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:32.000
I'm paying it forward even after I'm done living.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.320
And bone marrow is a truly life-saving substance,

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.980
used in treatments of a lot of cancers,

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.138
stuff like Leukemia,

00:13:38.138 --> 00:13:38.858
Lymphoma,

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:39.660
Sickle Cell Disease,

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.860
Aplastic Anemia,

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:45.060
While it may not be possible to sell your bone marrow in our non-Purge world,

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.500
you can donate it,

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.840
and in turn make a real difference today.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.200
So check out BeTheMatch.com,

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:54.580
or ask your doctor the next time you're in for a checkup,

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.480
how you can make our world a little less like the one in "The Purge"

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.680
Donating things like bone marrow, blood, make a huge difference.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.860
And you know what?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.700
Today we can all stand to be a little bit more compassionate to one another.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:09.880
You know, help make our world a little less like the one that we see in that fictional universe.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.380
Heh, man who knew that I would get so sappy

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:18.280
after an episode dedicated to ripping out the organs of other people in The Purge and profiting off of them.

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:20.449
Anyway, that's the theory!

00:14:20.449 --> 00:14:21.120
Aaaaand...

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:27.260
cut- up those dead bodies so you can go sell them for some big bucks in "The Purge" world, my friends!

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.980
Sorry, I couldn't stay serious for too long.

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:33.720
Have to end with some tongue-in-cheek cynical statement.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.200
But seriously, go donate blood.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.420
I'm looking to do it right now actually.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:42.440
Looking for a good place in the area, surprisingly difficult to find!

